### Bluenixx Build Manifest

Configure your git with your credentials.
example:

```
git config --global user.name "Your Name"
git config --global user.email "youremail@gmail.com"
```
Log in with your Google account on ![Android Google Source](https://android.googlesource.com/) and copy the code that appears, paste it into the terminal, and then you can start your build.

Remember, all of this only applies if you're using your own build server. If it's local, there are more things to configure. Read the ![Lineage OS](https://wiki.lineageos.org/) documentation.


Initialize the Repo:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/Bluenixx/bluenixx-manifest.git -b bluenixx-17.0 --git-lfs
```
Sync:
```
repo sync -c -j$(nproc --all) --force-sync --no-clone-bundle --no-tags
```

Then build Bluenixx:

```
source build/envsetup.sh
breakfast bangkk userdebug # or lunch lineage_bangkk-cp2a-userdebug
mka bacon -j$(nproc --all)
```

### Thank you for choosing Bluenixx!